You asked about surviving. My answer is simple: don't level up until you've
purchased all the protection you can get from the Minetown priest.

So of course that means that I always tackle the Mines first.

My early game is like a standard chess opening now:

1) Clean out the upper level shops in level 2-4
2) Level up to pet until it's large.
3) Take out only kobold zombies and possible newts. I'm running a monk now
so I don't even tackle the newts anymore.
4) Armor up as best as I can. I get a least a orcish helm before tackling
the Mines. In the Mines I usually put on whatever dead dwarves drops.
5) Get to the priest and pay to get my naked AC down to 1.
6) An addendum, ID as much stuff as I can.

Then and only then do I start levelling up myself. At that point my AC is
negative, the pet is really tough, and the monsters haven't graduated to
anything too terrible difficult at this point.

I'm only been playing a monk for a week. I finally ascended my Archeologist.
I've already gotten two monks deep into mid game. Their biggest problem is
food management due to meat eating guilt.

>Of course, Elbereth helps ;)

